                <pb facs="0815" n="808" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg808"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01 Provisional/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-14T18:00:00+08:00">December 14, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 14—7:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>825. My No. 820, December 14, 11 a.m.,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d899-f1"/> No. 822,
                    December 14, 4 p.m. I anticipate that within a few days I shall receive a call
                    from Wang Keh[-min] or some other representative or representatives of the new
                    Provisional Government. I should be greatly obliged if the Department would
                    instruct me specifically as to whether I should receive and return the call. In
                    view of the fact that this Embassy is senior Embassy of protocol [powers?] other
                    diplomatic representatives, judging by the past, may wish to follow the lead of
                    the Embassy in this matter. British representative has already informed me that,
                    unless he is instructed to the contrary, he will follow this Embassy’s lead.
                    Since the new régime claims to be the Provisional Government of China, an
                    important principle of policy, involving recognition, may be involved.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Ambassador.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
